# Glorious End cast on Bot1's own turn 1 ends it, and its "at the beginning of your next end step, you lose the game" waits
# for Bot1's next end step: not turn 1's, which is skipped (CR 724.1e), but turn 3's. There the ability triggers and is put
# on the stack, and Bot1 answers it with Time Stop, which exiles it with everything else on the stack (CR 724.1b). A
# delayed ability triggers only once (CR 603.7c): Bot1 does not lose then, nor at its end step on turn 5.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Glorious End
Time Stop
Island
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glorious End.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Exile = Glorious End
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Time Stop.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Result = InProgress
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
[T6 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Turn = 6
Result = InProgress
Bot1.Life = 20
Exile = Glorious End; Time Stop
